---
import SourcePanel from "./SourcePanel.astro";

const { topic, next, compact = false } = Astro.props;
const facts = [
  ["Within a Kalpa", "One of 14 Manvantaras"],
  ["Contains", "71 Maha Yugas"],
  ["Current era", "Vaivasvata Manvantara"],
  ["Current position", "7th Manvantara"],
];
const manus = [
  "Svayambhuva", "Svarocisa", "Uttama", "Tamasa", "Raivata", "Caksusa", "Vaivasvata",
  "Savarni", "Daksha Savarni", "Brahma Savarni", "Dharma Savarni", "Rudra Savarni", "Deva Savarni", "Indra Savarni",
];
const address = ["Universe", "Current Brahma", "Current Kalpa", "Vaivasvata Manvantara", "28th Maha Yuga", "Kali Yuga"];
---

<article class="manvantara-reading">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Cosmic Clock Project · Manvantara</p>
    <h1>The Age of a Manu</h1>
    <p class="lead">If human civilization unfolds through repeating cycles, who guides each new beginning?</p>
  </header>

  <dl class="facts">{facts.map(([label, value]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}</dl>

  <div class="reading-body"><main>
    <section>
      <h2>Every great era has a beginning</h2>
      <p>Imagine rebuilding the world after an age has ended.</p>
      <p>New generations are born. Societies begin again. Knowledge must be preserved. Laws must be taught. Civilization must find its direction.</p>
      <p>Who would guide such a new beginning?</p>
      <p>According to Hindu scriptures, every great age of humanity begins under the guidance of a figure known as <strong>Manu</strong>.</p>
      <p>His era is called a <strong>Manvantara</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is Manu?</h2>
      <p>The word Manu occupies a unique place in Hindu tradition.</p>
      <p>In many scriptural accounts, Manu is described as the progenitor of humanity, the one who establishes order for a new age after creation unfolds.</p>
      <p>He is not simply a king. Nor is he portrayed only as a teacher. Rather, Manu represents the beginning of a new human era.</p>
      <p>Each Manvantara has its own Manu. When one Manvantara ends, another begins with a different Manu.</p>
    </section>
  </main></div>

  <details class="full-guide" open={!compact} data-compact={compact || undefined}>
    <summary><span>Continue reading</span><b>Read full Manvantara guide</b></summary>
    <div class="reading-body"><main>
      <section>
        <h2>What is a Manvantara?</h2>
        <p>A Manvantara literally means <strong>the period of a Manu</strong>.</p>
        <p>It is one of the great divisions of cosmic time. During each Manvantara, the universe continues its ongoing cycle while humanity passes through many Maha Yugas under the guidance associated with that Manu.</p>
        <p>Think of it as a new chapter within the same cosmic day. The universe has not been recreated from nothing. Instead, a new era begins within an already existing cosmic cycle.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Imagine reading a book</h2>
        <p>A book may have many chapters. Each chapter introduces new people, new events, and new challenges.</p>
        <p>Yet the story continues.</p>
        <p>A Manvantara is similar. It is a new chapter in the cosmic story.</p>
        <p>The universe continues, but leadership, sages, and divine roles associated with that era are renewed according to traditional accounts.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The fourteen Manvantaras</h2>
        <p>According to Hindu cosmology, one daytime of Brahma contains fourteen Manvantaras.</p>
        <p>Each has its own Manu, its own Indra, a distinct group of sages known as Saptarishis, and different divine beings who play roles in maintaining cosmic order.</p>
        <p>This idea emphasizes that cosmic history is dynamic rather than static. Each age has its own unique identity.</p>
        <div class="manu-constellation" aria-label="Fourteen Manvantaras">
          {manus.map((manu, index) => <article class={index === 6 ? "manu-era current" : "manu-era"}><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><strong>{manu}</strong>{index === 6 && <small>You are here</small>}</article>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The structure of a Kalpa</h2>
        <p>A daytime of Brahma is traditionally divided into fourteen Manvantaras. Each Manvantara forms one major section of the cosmic day.</p>
        <aside class="note"><p class="eyebrow">Kalpa structure</p><p><strong>One day of Brahma</strong> contains <strong>14 Manvantaras</strong>. Each Manvantara contains <strong>71 Maha Yugas</strong>, with transitional periods described in the Puranic model.</p></aside>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Which Manvantara are we living in?</h2>
        <p>According to the traditional Puranic chronology, we are currently living in the <strong>Vaivasvata Manvantara</strong>.</p>
        <p>This is the seventh of the fourteen Manvantaras in the current Kalpa.</p>
        <p>The Manu of this era is Vaivasvata Manu, who is associated in several Hindu texts with preserving life through a great flood narrative.</p>
        <p>Within this Manvantara, the tradition further places us in the 28th Maha Yuga, specifically during Kali Yuga.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>A cosmic address</h2>
        <p>Think of it like a mailing address. Instead of house, street, city, and country, the cosmic address becomes:</p>
        <div class="address-map">{address.map((item, index) => <article class={item === "Vaivasvata Manvantara" ? "address-node current" : "address-node"}><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><strong>{item}</strong></article>)}</div>
        <p>Each level helps locate our place within the larger framework described by Hindu cosmology.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Did you know?</h2>
        <p>According to traditional calculations, <strong>71 Maha Yugas</strong> occur within one Manvantara, with transitional periods before and after each Manvantara as described in the Puranas.</p>
        <p>This shows how the cosmic calendar is built from repeating layers, each larger than the one before.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why does this matter?</h2>
        <p>The idea of the Manvantara expands our view of history.</p>
        <p>Instead of seeing civilization as one continuous story, Hindu cosmology presents it as a series of great eras.</p>
        <p>Each era begins with renewed guidance. Each contributes to the unfolding of the larger cosmic order.</p>
        <p>It is a reminder that, in this tradition, humanity's story is woven into a much broader cycle of time.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What comes next?</h2>
        <p>Now we know that four Yugas form a Maha Yuga, and many Maha Yugas unfold within a Manvantara.</p>
        <p>But another question naturally follows.</p>
        <p>What contains all fourteen Manvantaras?</p>
        <p>The answer is one of the most astonishing ideas in Hindu cosmology: the <strong>Kalpa</strong>, a single day of Brahma.</p>
      </section>

    </main></div>
    <SourcePanel sources={topic.data.sources} sourceNote={topic.data.sourceNote} traditionNote={topic.data.traditionNote} reviewedBy={topic.data.reviewedBy} lastReviewed={topic.data.lastReviewed} contentVersion={topic.data.contentVersion} />
  </details>

  <a class="continue" href={`/atlas/${next?.slug ?? "maha-yuga"}`}>
    <span><small>Ready to move deeper?</small><strong>Next: {next?.title ?? "Maha Yuga"}</strong><em>Discover the great cycle that repeats throughout every Manvantara.</em></span>
    <b>Explore next layer -></b>
  </a>
</article>

<style>
  .manvantara-reading{--accent:#65d7dc;color:#eee3cf}header,.reading-body,.facts,.manvantara-reading :global(.source-panel),.continue,.full-guide>summary{width:min(100% - 2rem,72rem);margin-inline:auto}
  header{padding:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem) 0 2.5rem}header p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:62ch;color:#b3aca1;line-height:1.85}header strong,.reading-body strong{color:var(--accent);font-weight:650}
  h1,h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0}h1{max-width:14ch;margin:.35rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,6rem);line-height:1}.lead{color:#d0c5b3!important;font-size:clamp(1.08rem,1.5vw,1.3rem)}
  .facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);border-block:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.2)}.facts div{padding:1rem}.facts div+div{border-left:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.14)}dt{color:#99938a;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}dd{margin:.25rem 0 0;color:#e5dac8;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem}
  .reading-body{padding-block:2rem}.reading-body main{width:min(100%,46rem)}section{border-bottom:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.14);padding-block:2rem}h2{margin:0 0 .8rem;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem);line-height:1.15}section p,section li{color:#aaa49a;line-height:1.85}section p{margin:.65rem 0 0}section em{color:#d3c9b9}.note{margin:1.5rem 0 0;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1rem}.note p{margin:.25rem 0;color:#c2b9aa}
  .manu-constellation{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem;margin:1.45rem 0 0}.manu-constellation::before{position:absolute;left:3%;right:3%;top:50%;height:1px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,rgb(101 215 220/.3),transparent);content:""}.manu-era{position:relative;z-index:1;display:grid;min-height:7.6rem;align-content:end;border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.16);border-radius:.85rem;padding:.72rem;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(101 215 220/.075),rgb(255 255 255/.018));overflow:hidden}.manu-era::before{position:absolute;top:.72rem;left:.72rem;width:.58rem;aspect-ratio:1;border-radius:50%;background:rgb(101 215 220/.45);box-shadow:0 0 18px rgb(101 215 220/.28);content:""}.manu-era span{color:#6faaa9;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em}.manu-era strong{margin-top:.3rem;color:#d5edef;font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.25}.manu-era small{width:max-content;margin-top:.38rem;border-radius:999px;padding:.22rem .42rem;background:var(--accent);color:#061217;font-size:.55rem;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase}.manu-era.current{border-color:rgb(101 215 220/.62);background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgb(101 215 220/.16),rgb(255 255 255/.028));box-shadow:0 0 34px rgb(101 215 220/.18),inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.08)}.manu-era.current::before{background:#d9ffff;box-shadow:0 0 24px rgb(101 215 220/.7)}
  .address-map{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem;margin:1.35rem 0}.address-node{position:relative;display:grid;gap:.35rem;min-height:5.7rem;align-content:center;border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.14);border-radius:.85rem;padding:.82rem;background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(101 215 220/.055),rgb(255 255 255/.018))}.address-node:not(:last-child)::after{position:absolute;right:-.48rem;top:50%;width:.38rem;height:1px;background:rgb(101 215 220/.35);content:""}.address-node span{color:#6faaa9;font-size:.62rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em}.address-node strong{color:#d5edef;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.25}.address-node.current{border-color:rgb(101 215 220/.48);background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(101 215 220/.13),rgb(255 255 255/.024));box-shadow:0 0 26px rgb(101 215 220/.13)}
  .full-guide{border:0}.full-guide:not([data-compact])>summary{display:none}.full-guide>summary{display:flex;width:fit-content;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;margin-top:.9rem;border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.25);border-radius:999px;padding:.55rem .8rem;background:rgb(101 215 220/.035);color:var(--accent);cursor:pointer;list-style:none}.full-guide>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.full-guide>summary span{color:#99938a;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.full-guide>summary b{font-size:.67rem}.full-guide[open]>summary b{font-size:0}.full-guide[open]>summary b::after{font-size:.67rem;content:"Hide full guide"}.full-guide[open]>.reading-body{animation:guide-reveal 420ms ease both}
  .continue{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;margin-top:2rem;border:1px solid rgb(199 140 255/.22);border-radius:1rem;padding:1.2rem 1.35rem;background:linear-gradient(100deg,rgb(199 140 255/.055),transparent);color:#c78cff}.continue span>*{display:block}.continue small{color:#99938a;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}.continue strong{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;font-weight:400}.continue em{color:#aaa49a;font-size:.72rem;font-style:normal}.continue b{font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase}
  .manvantara-reading{border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.2);border-radius:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem;background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(8 30 37/.72),rgb(3 13 20/.48));box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035),0 24px 80px rgb(0 0 0/.22);backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(115%)}
  .facts{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.2);border-radius:1rem;background:rgb(255 255 255/.025);box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
  .note,.manu-era,.address-node,.continue,.full-guide>summary{box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
  @keyframes guide-reveal{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(-8px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}
  @media(max-width:900px){.manu-constellation{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}.address-map{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.address-node:nth-child(3)::after{display:none}}
  @media(max-width:800px){.facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.facts div:nth-child(odd){border-left:0}.facts div:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.14)}.continue{align-items:flex-end}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.manu-constellation,.address-map{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.manu-era{min-height:6.5rem}.address-node:not(:last-child)::after{display:none}.continue{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}}

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-constellation) {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important;
    gap: .7rem !important;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0 !important;
    padding: 1rem !important;
    border: 1px solid rgb(101 215 220 / .16) !important;
    border-radius: 1rem !important;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgb(101 215 220 / .12), transparent 18rem), rgb(255 255 255 / .018) !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-era) {
    display: grid !important;
    min-height: 7.25rem !important;
    align-content: end !important;
    border: 1px solid rgb(101 215 220 / .18) !important;
    border-radius: .85rem !important;
    padding: .8rem !important;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(101 215 220 / .085), rgb(255 255 255 / .018)) !important;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255 / .035) !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-era span),
  :global(.manvantara-reading .address-node span) {
    display: block !important;
    color: #79dfe1 !important;
    font-size: .66rem !important;
    font-weight: 900 !important;
    letter-spacing: .12em !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-era strong),
  :global(.manvantara-reading .address-node strong) {
    display: block !important;
    margin-top: .35rem !important;
    color: #e4ffff !important;
    font-size: .82rem !important;
    line-height: 1.25 !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-era small) {
    display: inline-flex !important;
    width: max-content !important;
    margin-top: .45rem !important;
    border-radius: 999px !important;
    padding: .23rem .48rem !important;
    background: #65d7dc !important;
    color: #061217 !important;
    font-size: .55rem !important;
    font-weight: 900 !important;
    text-transform: uppercase !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-era.current) {
    border-color: rgb(101 215 220 / .72) !important;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(101 215 220 / .2), rgb(255 255 255 / .03)) !important;
    box-shadow: 0 0 36px rgb(101 215 220 / .22), inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255 / .08) !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .address-map) {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important;
    gap: .65rem !important;
    margin: 1.45rem 0 !important;
    padding: 1rem !important;
    border: 1px solid rgb(101 215 220 / .16) !important;
    border-radius: 1rem !important;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgb(101 215 220 / .06), rgb(255 255 255 / .018)) !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .address-node) {
    display: grid !important;
    min-height: 5.5rem !important;
    align-content: center !important;
    border: 1px solid rgb(101 215 220 / .16) !important;
    border-radius: .85rem !important;
    padding: .85rem !important;
    background: rgb(2 12 18 / .46) !important;
  }

  :global(.manvantara-reading .address-node.current) {
    border-color: rgb(101 215 220 / .58) !important;
    background: rgb(101 215 220 / .1) !important;
    box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgb(101 215 220 / .16) !important;
  }

  @media(max-width: 900px) {
    :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-constellation) { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important; }
    :global(.manvantara-reading .address-map) { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important; }
  }

  @media(max-width: 620px) {
    :global(.manvantara-reading .manu-constellation),
    :global(.manvantara-reading .address-map) { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr !important; }
  }
</style>